WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.357
Now connect the code to the visual.

00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:09.942
Sales is one thousand dollars, costs are eight hundred dollars, and profit becomes two hundred dollars.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:13.732
The key idea is that profit was not directly entered.

00:00:13.732 --> 00:00:16.352
We created it from the other values.

00:00:16.352 --> 00:00:18.479
That makes it a derived metric.

00:00:19.008 --> 00:00:21.675
Many familiar measures work the same way.

00:00:21.675 --> 00:00:29.100
Profit margin, growth rate, average order value, and conversion rate are all built from other values.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.040
If you change sales or costs, the profit bar should move too.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.528
That visual connection helps reinforce how inputs drive derived metrics.
